 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How to read a job advert",
     "texto": [
      "Many adverts use **se** so they do not name the company: **se busca una persona**, **se buscan dos personas**. The verb agrees with what comes next: **se requiere experiencia**, **se requieren dos años de experiencia**.\n\nA vacancy may ask for **experiencia**, **formación**, languages or **disponibilidad**, and offer a **contrato**, a **sueldo**, **horario flexible** or the chance of **ascenso**.\n\nTo get the job: **enviar el currículum**, **acudir a una entrevista** and, if they choose you, **firmar el contrato**. Later they may **despedirte**, or you may **dimitir** or **jubilarte**.\n\nA worker can be **empleado**, **autónomo** (self-employed), **funcionario** (in public administration) or **estudiante en prácticas**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "The «se» of adverts and «para quien»",
     "texto": [
      "In adverts, **se** + verb hides who is speaking. The verb agrees with the noun that follows:\n\n- **Se busca** una persona (singular).\n- **Se buscan** dos personas (plural).\n\nIf you talk about someone you do not know yet, after **quien** or **para quien** comes the subjunctive: **Hay ascenso para quien demuestre interés**.\n\nWatch **despedir**: it changes e to i in **despido**, **despides**, **despide**, **despiden**, but not in **despedimos**."
     ],
